{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385519-namtaru","id":1385519,"title":"Namtaru","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T19:43:05-07:00","id":1385519,"title":"Namtaru","content":"According to the lore, Nergal unearthed Namtaru beneath Chorazin, then moved it to the labyrinth beneath Knossos.<br /> <br /> Later, in 636 C.E. Assamites waged a war against the Baali at Chorazin. There, Izhim abd'Azrael and 12 other Assamites were absorbed into the colossal hand of Namtaru as part of a ritual.<br /> <br /> Later, in 1242 C.E. Izhim was freed by his childe Enkara from Namtaru. Izhim called Namtaru \u201cThe Fallen One&quot; and said that &quot;Namtaru&quot; was merely a word used in a futile effort to contain the infinite.<br /> <br /> So, if Nergal moved Namtaru from Chorazin to Knossos prior to the eruption of Thera in 1500 B.C., how is Namtaru still in Chorazin when the assamites go there in 636 C.E. and later in 1242 C.E.?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m interested in your theories. I personally think Namtaru refers not to a single entity, but all of the \u201cChildren\u201c that the Baali worship (I know of the Decani and I don\u2019t think it refers to them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T21:46:59-07:00","id":1385535,"title":"","content":"I don't have all my copies of the books anymore, so I can't say that I can recall whether somebody put some effort into cleaning the timeline up, but the sequence of events given on the White Wolf Fandom Wiki goes like this:<br /> <br /> Namtaru is discovered at Mashkan-Shapir, which was a real city in what is now Iraq.<br /> <br /> Nergal moves the beast to Knossos, a real city on the isle of Crete, and there loses Namtaru at the end of the Second Baali War.<br /> <br /> Namtaru later mysteriously turns up in Chorazin, a real city off the shore of the Sea of Galilee in what is now northern Israel.<br /> <br /> I have a nagging feeling that the initial discovery of Namtaru was moved from Chorazin to Mashkan-Shapir in a retcon. Maybe Chorazin is just the only place name that I'm remembering from the Baali's Dark Ages Clanbook, or maybe someone at either White Wolf or Onyx Path caught the issue you're describing and put in the effort to fix it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-04-2020, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T22:25:10-07:00","id":1385539,"title":"","content":"Maybe only a fragment of Namtaru was moved, the Hand. Or as mentioned Namtaru is the Children as a host, and maybe then a facet of Namtaru was discovered in Crete.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then there is the Idea that Namtaru was an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> I wonder what if the Aralu in the Ghost City of Enoch were just three Children Sarcaphagi, which is odd if you consider maybe the Children are the Earthly Bodies of the Malfeans, which reminds me of Bloodborne and how the Great Ones have a Mortal slumbering Corpse while their mind resides in the Dreamland. Or in Analects of the Third Garden the emanations of Ialdabaoth were knocked into slumber by Let Their Be Light. This fits Namtaru being the Fallen One, so if not a fallen Angel then it could be a fallen aspect/emanation of Ialdabaoth the anti-god.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T23:45:55-07:00","id":1385551,"title":"","content":"Framing the Children as qlippothic things from before Fiat Lux would do a lot to help sort out the crowded and self-contradictory taxonomy of demon types that built up in White Wolf's books over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T00:13:12-07:00","id":1385554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385519-namtaru?p=1385551#post1385551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Framing the Children as qlippothic things from before Fiat Lux would do a lot to help sort out the crowded and self-contradictory taxonomy of demon types that built up in White Wolf's books over the years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially considering Vampire seems to have generic Christian Demons that aren't really fleshed out because they are default media devils, while the rest of the setting already covered that area a number of different ways. Got convoluted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T04:37:25-07:00","id":1385582,"title":"","content":"I agree with the Malfeans theory.<br /> A lot of time ago there was a canon statement in Mage about what the Nephandi were worshipping. Basically the evil gods are the dreams of the Neverborns; and given how similar the Nephandi and the Baali are I can totally see how Namtaru might be an emanation of the Neverborns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T04:48:16-07:00","id":1385583,"title":"","content":"This is fascinating. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T04:56:09-07:00","id":1385584,"title":"","content":"From the Book of Madness<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BIGGER PROBLEMS<br /> Hard as it may be to believe, the Nephandi have<br /> other pressing concerns besides the relentless pressure<br /> of the Ascension War. Malfean Nephandi time and<br /> again find themselves charging into conflicts originated<br /> by their allies, often fighting to hold off angered<br /> spirits and shapeshifters while the tainted werewolves<br /> who started the conflict are long gone. Tensions between<br /> the two groups have been steadily rising for some<br /> time, exacerbated, some Malfeans claim, by the actions<br /> of other factions of Nephandi.<br /> However, there are other Malfeans to worry about,<br /> namely, the greatest and most powerful Spectres. Dwelling<br /> in a Labyrinth of their own gnawing, these servants<br /> of Oblivion (not the Wyrm) devote themselves to the<br /> corruption of the living and the dead, at least when they<br /> can rouse themselves from fitful slumber.<br /> <br /> DEAD THINGS<br /> <b>Far worse, however, are the true Malfeans \u2014<br /> the ageless Never-born Spectres who sleep uneasily<br /> at the heart of the Underworld's Labyrinth,</b><br /> <b>Created when Entropy was born, these creatures<br /> gnawed the endlessly shifting corridors of the First<br /> Labyrinth from the raw stuff of Creation.</b> Now,<br /> they slumber restlessly in the chambers and halls<br /> they've carved out for themselves, dreaming dreams<br /> of power and destruction.<br /> Such dreams concern the Nephandi, and with<br /> good reason. The uncanny number of coincidences<br /> between the geography of the Underworld and the<br /> Nephandi's own paradigm has raised many questions.<br /> Recently, much to their regret, a team of<br /> Infernalist researchers set out to discover the truth<br /> behind this uncanny resonance.<br /> The conclusions that this research team reached<br /> both frightened and angered the reigning gilledeans<br /> \u2014 and their Masters. Not one of the researchers<br /> outlived his initial presentation of the team's findings<br /> by more than five minutes, and every report,<br /> note or voice recording made during the course of<br /> the study found itself consigned to the fire. At least,<br /> that was the fate of all of the research materials that<br /> could be found. Certain materials, smuggled out by<br /> Void Engineer barabbi to Convention acquaintances,<br /> revealed the chilling truth.<br /> <b>In essence, the report claimed that the entities<br /> the Nephandi serve are nothing more than the<br /> dreams of the sleeping Malfeans in the primal Labyrinth.<br /> The Labyrinths, titles and natures of all that<br /> dwell Beyond are reflections and sleep-distorted<br /> versions of the thoughts flickering through the<br /> sleeping minds of the Never-born.</b> And, when one<br /> of the sleeping Malfeans awakens, much that he<br /> dreams vanishes.<br /> Both fear and excitement have sprung from this<br /> last point, particularly among Technocratic mages<br /> and the restless dead who spy on them. Researches<br /> into the Shadowlands indicate that the oldest and<br /> most powerful Malfean, Gorool, awakened just as<br /> the Technocracy and Traditions commenced their<br /> final assault on the Nephandi in 1945. Observers<br /> from both groups remarked at the time that the<br /> defending Nephandi seemed confused and weakened,<br /> and many called on powers or allies that never<br /> materialized. The implication of all this is that<br /> Gorool's awakening destroyed his dreaming creations,<br /> depriving those who served those dreams of<br /> power in their hour of need.<br /> Even now, a report from a gang of ghostly spies<br /> sits on the desk of the Skeletal Lord of the dead.<br /> Inside are the details of a proposed invasion of the<br /> Labyrinth by a multi-Convention strike force. The<br /> assault's stated purpose is simple: To awaken the<br /> slumbering Malfeans, thus perilously weakening the<br /> resurgent Nephandi. As for the effect that this tactic<br /> would have on the Shadowlands, the Technocratic<br /> assessment is chillingly simple: unimportant.<br /> Worse still, though, are those Nephandi who<br /> have heard snippets of this research, and come to<br /> the conclusion that if they are only worshippers of<br /> dreams of true outer darkness, then how much more<br /> powerful could they be if they worshipped the things<br /> that dreamed such horrors into existence? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Now while it's true that this is a Mage thing (even still, it's a very cross-over Mage thing) it's stillthe best cosmological explanation about evil entities in the World of Darkness. In this way the Neverborn and Oblivion become the source of every dark god, wyrm or anything.<br /> <br /> Some fan on Werewolf hate this book because it makes the Wyrm an emanation of the Neverborns and Oblivion, but I think that a miscarried universe that predates the very notion of existence, something that never was (in a time were &quot;time&quot; wasn't, and &quot;was&quot; was a meaningless concept) and &quot;was&quot; before the Fiat Lux, is an excellent source for a &quot;Unified Evil Theory&quot;<br /> <br /> It really does make much easier to fit Yama Kings, Maeljin, Wyrm, Demon Lords (and even the Fallen, with a bit of work) into one cosmology.<br /> Especially because it doesn't make one religion true (like Demon the Fallen did), since while we could describe it as a Qlipphot, and use terms and nouns from the Qabbala and western mysticism, it's just a mere attempt of human minds to describe something that cannot be described. You could use any system of belief to encapsulate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 05-04-2020, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T10:17:34-07:00","id":1385615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385519-namtaru?p=1385584#post1385584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now while it's true that this is a Mage thing (even still, it's a very cross-over Mage thing) it's stillthe best cosmological explanation about evil entities in the World of Darkness. In this way the Neverborn and Oblivion become the source of every dark god, wyrm or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to get even more interesting (and make things easier on the Werewolf fans) throw in the truths learned about Oblivion in Orpheus; that Oblivion is a lie. If it were really capable of consuming everything it would have already done so.<br /> <br /> In truth Oblivion is actually creation\u2019s recycling system buried at the bottom of the great weave of creation and the event horizon is the boundaries of its prison. Everything that falls in actually comes out somewhere and in some fashion. The Neverborn are aspects of Oblivion which have escaped that prison and, whenever they\u2019re awake, seek to free Oblivion and loose it upon Creation.<br /> <br /> Doesn\u2019t that sound suspiciously like the Wyrm captured at the of the Weave of Creation and heads of the Hydra seeking to free the Wyrm from the clutches of the Weaver?<br /> <br /> The Triatic Wyrm was part of the natural cycle; recycling the old so that it could be born anew by the Wyld and then woven into patterns by the Weaver. Oblivion was originally part of the natural cycle; recycling old spirits so new lives could be born. The Weaver bound the Wyrm into its creation and the Wyrm shredded itself into the Hydra trying to free itself. Oblivion too shredded parts of itself into the Neverborn to escape its prison.<br /> <br /> Thus, the True Wyrm and Oblivion are one and the same entity. The Neverborn/Maeljin/Yama Kings are the same entities viewed through different lens.<br /> <br /> Then... if you want to go even more wild with it tag in Mage\u2019s belief creates reality and bygones/marauders being unable to enter a reality that no longer supports them.<br /> <br /> Bygones are thaumivores. They need to spend a point of quintessence every day to remain in the mortal world and possess various powers that ignore paradox. Vampires need to spend a blood point (valued at one quintessence in Mage) each night to remain active in the mortal world and possess various powers that ignore paradox.<br /> <br /> Vampires have ancients that slumber in secret places and wish to consume, at the least, their progeny when they wake. The Neverborn are ancient spirits that slumber in secret places and wish to consume the world when they wake.<br /> <br /> At one point in the distant past of Mage/Werewolf/Changeling there was a time when there was no difference between the mortal and spirit worlds, including the realms of the dead. Demon makes a point to there being different layers of reality... one where Caine is a lone man who killed his brother Abel, one where he is a clan of early agricultural humans who warred with the hunter/gatherers and other layers besides.<br /> <br /> What if the legends of Caine and the Antediluvians are just a layer of reality that overlays the deeper layer that is the very concept of murder/destruction/Oblivion and its poisonous fruits/Neverborn/Antediluvians... and the vampiric condition is but a spiritual reflection of this primordial reality that sustains itself as all thaumivores do, by consuming quintessence that it has ripped from the very life blood of mortals?<br /> <br /> Just how deep do you wish to dig for truth? How deep before the madness consumes you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T15:04:09-07:00","id":1385663,"title":"","content":"This stuff is amazing! Cosmologically speaking. Thank you guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T15:31:39-07:00","id":1385667,"title":"","content":"I think we should remember the simple explanation for the Baalis slumbering children, who howled and burned when exposed to the light. That they were ancient Vampires and that the Baali has been someones patsies since long before they were embraced and that everything they believe is a lie they've been told.<br /> <br /> But yes, I am really enjoying the cosmological alternatives to &quot;vampires lie&quot;, they are good<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T18:32:46-07:00","id":1385703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385519-namtaru?p=1385663#post1385663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This stuff is amazing! Cosmologically speaking. Thank you guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it\u2019s been a year ago, here\u2019s a post I did that first explored some of the Orpheus/Oblivion/Wyrm connections;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1295832-removing-grimderp?p=1296162#post1296162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main way I dealt with it in my Mage campaign was to take one of the elements of Orpheus and run with it; Oblivion is a LIE. The idea that all of Creation can be undone is the Nephandic equivalent of a fairy tale. In one campaign the PCs were investigating and ended up on the edge of Oblivion itself... specifically at the spiritual embodiment of the Fallen Tower which was a Nephandic holy site that leaned out over the maw of Oblivion). What they learned through ancient writings on the walls is that the Oblivion was a myth created by the first Neverborn Malfeans..the first beings to reach its edge and falter in primal fear at the gateway to the unknown. This myth of eternal destruction filtered up to other spirits of the dead and the practices of Mages who associated with the dead and over time was corrupted by angry outcasts mages into a nihilistic credo that became the first Nephandi.<br /> <br /> It filtered up to the Fera as well in the story that the Primeval Wyrm had gone insane and was now consuming everything.<br /> <br /> The Nephandic Cauls, the Black Spiral, the Banes and corruption spirits all grew from the power of belief in this lie and further hiding the truth.<br /> <br /> The Truth? Oblivion/the Wyrm is what it has always been... the portal to birth/rebirth and the transition from one life to the next. The primal fear of the Neverborn is the fear of an infant being born from the safety of its mother\u2019s womb, the only existence it has ever known, into the bright, cold uncertain world beyond.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn are literally the \u201cnever born.\u201d Primeval miscarriages whose spirits were too afraid of birth and even more terrified of the unknowns of rebirth to pass through \u201cOblivion\u2019s\u201d maw and so are stuck in a stasis of their own making.<br /> <br /> The greatest irony is that the corruption the werewolves are fighting isn\u2019t actually the Wyrm at all. It\u2019s just the natural side effect of the Weaver\u2019s efforts to keep the current world from sliding into the maw of Rebirth.<br /> <br /> By defying the natural pull of entropy, the Wraith Hierarchy, the Weaver Spirits (embodying man\u2019s primal desire for a stable and knowable world... a fear of chaos and the unknown), the static vampires and the Technocracy all must build ever more elaborate constructs and schemes to keep it from all tumbling down... and it is the imperfections in this ever more rickety structure and compromises needed to keep it all afloat that creates the corruption the werewolves sense as The Wyrm.<br /> <br /> What the werewolves are actually fighting is not the True Wyrm, but the corruption in the construct built by Man to protect itself from the very primal fears of corruption/oblivion placed in them by the Impergium. The Nephandi are lunatics who drive themselves insane because their exposure to \u201cThe Truth\u201d instills in them not a desire to clear away the rot so there\u2019s room for new growth, but a nihilistic desire to \u201ctear it all down.\u201d<br /> <br /> Both the Banes and the Nephandi are self-destructive messes because they are NOT actually any sort of cosmic force of oblivion.<br /> <br /> The banes the werewolves fight are the natural corruption of a system that has grown to stagnant (like papering over the dry rot or applying another layer of bondo and paint to the rust on a car), but corruption keeps growing because the wolves are so focused on the symptoms, they can\u2019t see the disease (i.e. the stagnation of the world) and even more that THEY are actually the root cause of that disease (the world stagnates because of its overwhelming fear of the unknown... of the monsters that lurk there and prey upon them... in short, the werewolves from days past).<br /> <br /> The Nephandi are the people who react to a cancer diagnosis by trying to kill themselves to just get it over with instead of devoting the time and energy it would take to actually cleanse the body of the poisons.<br /> <br /> In other words, the actual means of restoring the cosmic balance is to stop fighting \u201cOblivion\u201d and allow the dead and corrupt to be consumed so they can be reborn. The hunt to destroy the \u201cWyrm-taint\u201d and the Nephandi are just the two opposite extremes of dealing with it (\u201cignore it and hope it goes away\u201d and \u201cburn it all down\u201d respectively).</div> </div> </div> </div>This was before I got into the Demon \u201clayers of reality\u201d aspect where concepts (murder) are people (Caine) are groups (early agricultural tribes) depending on the layer of reality you\u2019re looking at. With that added in I think you could easily make the case that the very concept of the Antediluvians is synonymous with the Neverborn and Maeljin and the Yama Kings... it all just depends on which of the infinite layers of reality you\u2019re looking at.<br /> <br /> This also might explain why there can be anywhere from 13 (three and ten) and 30 (three tens) of Antediluvians and its NOT a translation error... it\u2019s a layer of reality viewpoint error. Caine is a singular vampire god who ruled a single advanced First City on one level while on another he\u2019s the entire vampire race who descended in ones and twos upon many of the first communities as they moved into an agrarian society.<br /> <br /> In that sense it could be that Caine is the Antediluvians and the Antediluvians are Caine. Did the angels/spirits curse a single man (Caine) or an entire tribe (the Antediluvians)? Was Caine even a vampire at all or was his vision of the three angels merely the result of a very bad forced Awakening by Lilith and the vampiric state a contagious permanent paradox flaw that accompanied his paradigm of blood magic? Is the reason it is said that the Antediluvians can never die because of the vampiric curse -or- is it because they\u2019re already dead and are now the Onceborn Malfeans sleeping in the Labryinth and whose dreams manifest as monsters like Ravnos during the Week of Nightmares?<br /> <br /> All sorts of ways you could take things if you choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T19:49:55-07:00","id":1385718,"title":"","content":"Wow!!! I have trouble with abstract concepts, but I still love the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:58:40-07:00","id":1385742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385519-namtaru?p=1385615#post1385615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to get even more interesting (and make things easier on the Werewolf fans) throw in the truths learned about Oblivion in Orpheus; that Oblivion is a lie. If it were really capable of consuming everything it would have already done so.<br /> <br /> In truth Oblivion is actually creation\u2019s recycling system buried at the bottom of the great weave of creation and the event horizon is the boundaries of its prison. Everything that falls in actually comes out somewhere and in some fashion. The Neverborn are aspects of Oblivion which have escaped that prison and, whenever they\u2019re awake, seek to free Oblivion and loose it upon Creation.<br /> <br /> Doesn\u2019t that sound suspiciously like the Wyrm captured at the of the Weave of Creation and heads of the Hydra seeking to free the Wyrm from the clutches of the Weaver?<br /> <br /> The Triatic Wyrm was part of the natural cycle; recycling the old so that it could be born anew by the Wyld and then woven into patterns by the Weaver. Oblivion was originally part of the natural cycle; recycling old spirits so new lives could be born. The Weaver bound the Wyrm into its creation and the Wyrm shredded itself into the Hydra trying to free itself. Oblivion too shredded parts of itself into the Neverborn to escape its prison.<br /> <br /> Thus, the True Wyrm and Oblivion are one and the same entity. The Neverborn/Maeljin/Yama Kings are the same entities viewed through different lens.<br /> <br /> Then... if you want to go even more wild with it tag in Mage\u2019s belief creates reality and bygones/marauders being unable to enter a reality that no longer supports them.<br /> <br /> Bygones are thaumivores. They need to spend a point of quintessence every day to remain in the mortal world and possess various powers that ignore paradox. Vampires need to spend a blood point (valued at one quintessence in Mage) each night to remain active in the mortal world and possess various powers that ignore paradox.<br /> <br /> Vampires have ancients that slumber in secret places and wish to consume, at the least, their progeny when they wake. The Neverborn are ancient spirits that slumber in secret places and wish to consume the world when they wake.<br /> <br /> At one point in the distant past of Mage/Werewolf/Changeling there was a time when there was no difference between the mortal and spirit worlds, including the realms of the dead. Demon makes a point to there being different layers of reality... one where Caine is a lone man who killed his brother Abel, one where he is a clan of early agricultural humans who warred with the hunter/gatherers and other layers besides.<br /> <br /> What if the legends of Caine and the Antediluvians are just a layer of reality that overlays the deeper layer that is the very concept of murder/destruction/Oblivion and its poisonous fruits/Neverborn/Antediluvians... and the vampiric condition is but a spiritual reflection of this primordial reality that sustains itself as all thaumivores do, by consuming quintessence that it has ripped from the very life blood of mortals?<br /> <br /> Just how deep do you wish to dig for truth? How deep before the madness consumes you?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this fits with my Headcanon that Apep is the Oblivion aspected head of the Wyrm, but the thing is the Wyrm's three heads are on the other side, so this makes Apep the Wyrm's Anus/Tail and its mouth is Oblivion. And Ma'at is the last remaining vestige of the Balance Wyrm on Earth, with the Elder Serpent in Pangaea being the Ouroboros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T21:59:59-07:00","id":1385744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385519-namtaru?p=1385667#post1385667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we should remember the simple explanation for the Baalis slumbering children, who howled and burned when exposed to the light. That they were ancient Vampires and that the Baali has been someones patsies since long before they were embraced and that everything they believe is a lie they've been told.<br /> <br /> But yes, I am really enjoying the cosmological alternatives to &quot;vampires lie&quot;, they are good<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean they are Older then Caine? Or do you think they are 2nd/3rd gens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T23:01:17-07:00","id":1385751,"title":"","content":"There's a ton of things you can do with the Children, and I've done a couple of different things with them over the years.<br /> <br /> In one, a more recent V20 Tal'mahe'ra game, I had them as funky vampires sired by Caine - he needed Lilith's help to create the 2nd Generation (which in turn created the 3rd generation and so on). Later, after a falling out between the two, Caine began embracing some Lilith's inhuman children. The result were these weird immensely powerful vampires gone wrong that were stuck in perpetual frenzy. Lilith ended up lulling them to sleep because she didn't want to kill them and the Baali worshippers ended up discovering them.<br /> <br /> In another campaign in which three of the players were Lasombra and one of them had a heavy focus on Abyss Sorcery, I had the Children function as creatures had emerged from the Abyss (the funky place Lasombra can go to) and I had the Baali as a clan created by Lasombra. It didn't end up playing a huge role in the campaign, but was just kind of a side note the players came across. Then in a Mage game that was focusing heavily on the Underworld, I had it so that the Children were the physical corpses of Onceborn (Oneborn are immensely powerful spectres in Wraith that serve Oblivion) which had been twisted post-mortem by the soul's closeness to Oblivion. The players had to go unearth one of the Children to get a the body of the Onceborn they were dealing with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T03:06:48-07:00","id":1385788,"title":"","content":"On a side note, Chris' idea of the Antedeluvians as creatures stuck in stasis because they fear death and rebirth goes very well with the ending of Netflix's recent Dracula miniseries. It fits like a glove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T11:12:51-07:00","id":1385876,"title":"","content":"As soon as I get my laptop back from being repaired I\u2019ll add some more stuff I had on this (on my phone currently).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T08:18:31-07:00","id":1386085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385519-namtaru?p=1385744#post1385744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean they are Older then Caine? Or do you think they are 2nd/3rd gens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe third or possibly generation, kindred from before the flood. Gone into torpor when the world was covered with ocean, and buried in a thin layer of sediment. Then the flood receeded, and men covered the land again. And one tribe dug into the tomb of these creatures in the middle of the day. And it burned.<br /> <br /> Some time after the flood, even Antediluvian creatures were much younger and with less power to act in torpor or resist the noonday sun. So the others lied to the first tribe. Told them stories of what they were and why they needed the blood-drenched rituals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T09:23:33-07:00","id":1387286,"title":"","content":"So, if the Kindred are the constructs of the Neverborn -- and the Neverborn are entities from the beginning of time that balked at being recycled -- then that could make the kindred tools created by the Neverborn to serve as anchor points for reality. The kindred are living stasis, and their existence helps root reality in place so that reality doesnt fall further towards the recycle point. Metaphorically, they are stakes driven into the ground in an attempt to avoid further erosion.<br /> <br /> Which could also explain the way generation works. When the Neverborn created Caine or the first Kindred, they embued a lot of &quot;stasis&quot; into those vampires. These handful of Kindred were expected to magically hold reality where it is by their very existence. The diffusion of Kindred stasis powers is reflected in Generation. The same amount of stasis power exists, but over time has diffused to a larger group with lesser stasis power. This works to the Neverborn demons' advantage because their Kindred-anchors are now spread farther afield throughout reality, lessening the chance that some part of the reality slips through the cracks as well as ensuring that the loss of one, or even hundreds, of the Kindred-anchors isnt devastating.<br /> <br /> This also explains why you cant turn a Vampire into a chair via reality magick... Kindred essence stands outside of reality. The Kindred's being is designed to affect reality on a fundamental level... something deeper than even what Willworker can manipulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 05-10-2020, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T12:15:56-07:00","id":1387307,"title":"","content":"Where you're going with that is interesting. It wouldn't take too much effort to connect changelings' perception of vampires as sources of Banality to this idea of vampires as Stasis creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}